---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="ProofDesk Intake — Next Steps" description="Submit your evidence materials for AnchorForge ProofDesk intake. Learn what to send, how to package it, turnaround windows, and what happens next.">

<section style="padding-top: 180px; min-height: 80vh;">
  <div class="container narrow" style="max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 5vw;">

    <!-- HERO -->
    <div class="eyebrow">ProofDesk Intake</div>
    <h1 class="pd-h1">Your ProofDesk run<br>has started.</h1>
    <p class="pd-sub">Now send the folder. We'll turn the mess into a sealed review packet another human can trust and inspect.</p>

    <div class="pd-cta-row">
      <a href="mailto:ProofDeskService@aiitcorp.com?subject=ProofDesk%20Intake" class="btn-buy">Email your evidence →</a>
      <a href="#what-to-send" class="pd-link">What should I send? ↓</a>
    </div>

    <p class="pd-note">Use the same email address you used at checkout if possible. If not, include your payment email in the message.</p>

    <!-- LAYER 1: IMMEDIATE NEXT STEPS -->
    <div class="pd-layer">
      <div class="eyebrow">Do these three things first</div>
      <div class="pd-cards-3">
        <div class="pd-card-num">
          <div class="pd-num">1</div>
          <h3>Email your intake</h3>
          <p>Send your evidence materials to <strong>ProofDeskService@aiitcorp.com</strong>.<br>Use subject line: <em>ProofDesk Intake — [Your Name / Project Name]</em>.</p>
          <a href="mailto:ProofDeskService@aiitcorp.com?subject=ProofDesk%20Intake%20%E2%80%94%20Project%20Name" class="pd-card-btn">Open email →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-card-num">
          <div class="pd-num">2</div>
          <h3>Attach the folder or link</h3>
          <p>One ZIP file is best. If the folder is too large for email, send a Google Drive, Dropbox, OneDrive, iCloud, or WeTransfer link with download access enabled.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-card-num">
          <div class="pd-num">3</div>
          <h3>Add a short note</h3>
          <p>Tell us what the packet is for: attorney review, investor review, client handoff, invention timeline, AI-output review, dispute prep, or something else.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- LAYER 2: WHAT TO SEND -->
    <div id="what-to-send" class="pd-layer">
      <div class="eyebrow">What to send us</div>
      <p class="pd-lead">Send the mess. Do not spend six hours making it pretty first. ProofDesk exists because evidence usually arrives messy.</p>

      <div class="pd-two-col">
        <div>
          <h4>Accepted materials</h4>
          <ul class="pd-checklist">
            <li>PDFs</li><li>Screenshots</li><li>Photos</li><li>Scans</li>
            <li>Word docs</li><li>Google Doc exports</li><li>Spreadsheets</li>
            <li>Emails or email exports</li><li>Receipts</li><li>Invoices</li>
            <li>Contracts</li><li>Code files</li><li>GitHub exports</li>
            <li>Logs</li><li>AI chats</li><li>Prompt/output records</li>
            <li>Citations</li><li>Timelines</li><li>Notes</li>
            <li>Audio/video transcripts</li><li>ZIP archives</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>Helpful context</h4>
          <ul class="pd-checklist pd-context">
            <li>What are you trying to prove?</li>
            <li>Who needs to review this?</li>
            <li>What is the deadline?</li>
            <li>Which files matter most?</li>
            <li>Which claims feel weakest?</li>
            <li>Are there known disputes or contradictions?</li>
            <li>Is anything confidential or sensitive?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- LAYER 3: FOLDER STRUCTURE -->
    <div class="pd-layer">
      <div class="eyebrow">If you want to organize it, use this structure</div>
      <p class="pd-lead">This is optional. If your folder is a mess, send it anyway.</p>

      <pre class="pd-tree">project-name/
  README-FIRST.txt
  claims/
  screenshots/
  citations/
  contracts/
  receipts/
  code/
  ai-outputs/
  emails/
  timelines/
  notes/
  raw/</pre>

      <a href="/proofdesk-intake-template.txt" download class="pd-card-btn" style="margin-top: 16px;">Download intake template →</a>
    </div>

    <!-- LAYER 4: LARGE FILES -->
    <div class="pd-layer">
      <div class="eyebrow">How to send large files</div>
      <div class="pd-cards-3">
        <div class="pd-card-num">
          <h3>Email attachment</h3>
          <p>Best for files under 25MB. Attach ZIP or individual files.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-card-num">
          <h3>Cloud folder link</h3>
          <p>Best for folders up to 10GB. Use Google Drive, Dropbox, OneDrive, iCloud, or WeTransfer. Make sure download access is enabled.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-card-num">
          <h3>Large or sensitive intake</h3>
          <p>For large, sensitive, or restricted evidence sets, email first with a short description. We'll coordinate a safer handoff path.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="pd-note">Recommended intake size: under 10GB. Larger packets accepted by coordination. A dedicated upload portal is planned. For now, email intake gives us the cleanest human review path.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- LAYER 5: WHAT HAPPENS NEXT -->
    <div class="pd-layer">
      <div class="eyebrow">What happens next</div>
      <div class="pd-steps">
        <div class="pd-step">
          <div class="pd-step-num">1</div>
          <div class="pd-step-body">
            <h3>Intake confirmation</h3>
            <p>We confirm receipt and make sure we can access the materials.</p>
            <div class="pd-timing">Starter / Founder / Binder: within 2 business hours<br>Emergency: priority confirmation during active coverage</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-step">
          <div class="pd-step-num">2</div>
          <div class="pd-step-body">
            <h3>Inventory</h3>
            <p>We index files, preserve originals, and generate the working manifest.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-step">
          <div class="pd-step-num">3</div>
          <div class="pd-step-body">
            <h3>Hash + custody</h3>
            <p>We generate SHA-256 checksums and write the chain-of-custody record.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-step">
          <div class="pd-step-num">4</div>
          <div class="pd-step-body">
            <h3>Claim review</h3>
            <p>We match claims to evidence, flag unsupported claims, and identify risk areas.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-step">
          <div class="pd-step-num">5</div>
          <div class="pd-step-body">
            <h3>Handoff packet</h3>
            <p>You receive a sealed archive with review memo, manifest, checksums, risk register, claim table, source copy, and optional print/binder package.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- LAYER 6: TURNAROUND -->
    <div class="pd-layer">
      <div class="eyebrow">Turnaround windows</div>
      <div class="pd-turnaround">
        <div class="pd-turn-row">
          <div class="pd-turn-tier"><strong>Starter Proof Seal</strong><span>3–5 business days</span></div>
          <div class="pd-turn-desc">Small folder. Fast seal. Clean receipts.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-turn-row">
          <div class="pd-turn-tier"><strong>Founder Review Packet</strong><span>2–3 business days</span></div>
          <div class="pd-turn-desc">Launch claims, investor packets, client work, and product evidence.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-turn-row">
          <div class="pd-turn-tier"><strong>Patent / AI Evidence Binder</strong><span>5–7 business days</span></div>
          <div class="pd-turn-desc">Invention timelines, AI-assisted research, technical claims, citations, screenshots, code, and chronology.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-turn-row pd-turn-rush">
          <div class="pd-turn-tier"><strong>Emergency ProofDesk Run</strong><span>24-hour priority target</span></div>
          <div class="pd-turn-desc">Urgent disputes, deadlines, takedowns, launches, and high-pressure evidence cleanup.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="pd-note">Turnaround depends on evidence volume, file access, and whether we need clarification.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- LAYER 7: WHAT YOU RECEIVE -->
    <div class="pd-layer">
      <div class="eyebrow">Your final packet</div>
      <div class="pd-outputs">
        <div class="pd-output"><strong>MANIFEST.tsv</strong><span>Every file indexed.</span></div>
        <div class="pd-output"><strong>SHA256SUMS.txt</strong><span>Cryptographic checksums for packet integrity.</span></div>
        <div class="pd-output"><strong>CHAIN_OF_CUSTODY.md</strong><span>When, where, and how the packet was assembled.</span></div>
        <div class="pd-output"><strong>CLAIM_REVIEW_TABLE.md</strong><span>Claims mapped against available source evidence.</span></div>
        <div class="pd-output"><strong>RISK_REGISTER.md</strong><span>Weak claims, missing evidence, contradictions, and uncertainty.</span></div>
        <div class="pd-output"><strong>HANDOFF_MEMO.md</strong><span>Plain-English summary for attorney, client, investor, reviewer, or partner.</span></div>
        <div class="pd-output"><strong>source/</strong><span>A preserved copy of the materials used.</span></div>
        <div class="pd-output"><strong>sealed .zip</strong><span>Final packet archive.</span></div>
        <div class="pd-output"><strong>optional binder</strong><span>Printable review packet if ordered or requested.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- LAYER 8: BOUNDARIES -->
    <div class="pd-layer">
      <div class="eyebrow">Important boundaries</div>
      <div class="pd-boundary">
        <p><strong>ProofDesk is proof operations.</strong></p>
        <p>It is not legal advice.<br>It is not patent filing.<br>It is not attorney representation.<br>It is not a guarantee that a claim is legally valid.</p>
        <p>We organize, hash, review, flag, summarize, and seal the evidence packet so the next human can inspect it faster.</p>
        <p>If you need legal advice, patent strategy, litigation support, or filing decisions, give the finished packet to a qualified attorney.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- LAYER 9: PRIVACY -->
    <div class="pd-layer">
      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy and retention</div>
      <div class="pd-privacy">
        <p>We handle evidence as operational material, not public content. Do not send materials you are not authorized to share. Tell us clearly if anything is confidential, privileged, export-controlled, or sensitive.</p>
        <p>Unless otherwise arranged, we retain working materials only as long as needed to complete the packet and resolve delivery/support issues.</p>
        <p><strong>For highly sensitive materials, contact us before sending files.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FINAL CTA -->
    <div class="pd-final">
      <h2>Bring the folder.<br>Leave with receipts.</h2>
      <a href="mailto:ProofDeskService@aiitcorp.com?subject=ProofDesk%20Intake" class="btn-buy">Email ProofDesk Intake →</a>
      <p class="pd-note" style="margin-top: 24px;">Questions or access issues? <a href="mailto:ProofDeskService@aiitcorp.com" style="color: var(--amber);">ProofDeskService@aiitcorp.com</a></p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .pd-h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.5vw, 4rem);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .pd-sub {
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.15rem);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .pd-cta-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .pd-link {
    color: var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.3);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
  }

  .pd-note {
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  .pd-layer {
    margin-top: 64px;
  }

  .pd-lead {
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .pd-cards-3 {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .pd-card-num {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
    border: 1px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.12);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 24px 20px;
  }

  .pd-card-num h3 {
    color: var(--cream, #E8E0D4);
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .pd-card-num p {
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .pd-card-num strong { color: var(--amber, #D4AF37); }
  .pd-card-num em { color: var(--cream, #E8E0D4); font-style: normal; }

  .pd-card-btn {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.3);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
  }

  .pd-num {
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .pd-two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .pd-two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .pd-two-col h4 {
    color: var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .pd-checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .pd-checklist li {
    padding: 4px 0;
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }

  .pd-context li {
    padding: 6px 0;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .pd-tree {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    border: 1px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.15);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    overflow-x: auto;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .pd-steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .pd-step {
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .pd-step-num {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .pd-step-body h3 {
    color: var(--cream, #E8E0D4);
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .pd-step-body p {
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .pd-timing {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .pd-turnaround {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .pd-turn-row {
    padding: 16px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
    border: 1px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.1);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .pd-turn-rush {
    border-color: var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    background: rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.06);
  }

  .pd-turn-tier {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .pd-turn-tier strong { color: var(--cream, #E8E0D4); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .pd-turn-tier span { color: var(--amber, #D4AF37); font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 0.8rem; }

  .pd-turn-desc {
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .pd-outputs {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .pd-output {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .pd-output strong {
    color: var(--amber, #D4AF37);
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .pd-output span {
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .pd-boundary {
    padding: 24px;
    border-left: 3px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.4);
    background: rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.04);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
  }

  .pd-boundary p {
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .pd-boundary p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .pd-boundary strong { color: var(--cream, #E8E0D4); }

  .pd-privacy {
    padding: 20px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
    border: 1px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.08);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .pd-privacy p {
    color: var(--slate, #8A9AB5);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .pd-privacy p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .pd-privacy strong { color: var(--cream, #E8E0D4); }

  .pd-final {
    margin-top: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 80px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .pd-final h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.5vw, 2rem);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
</style>

</Layout>
